ow program output and the log\\nprintf \"%s\\\\n\" \"=== /workspace/.env_log contents ===\" && cat /workspace/.env_log\\'\\ntest program ran\\n=== /workspace/.env_log contents ===\\nHOME=/root\\nSHELL=/bin/bash\\nPATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin\\nNO_SUCH_VAR=(null)', command='bash -lc \\'set -euo pipefail\\n# Compile the shared library\\ngcc -fPIC -shared -o /workspace/env_hook.so /workspace/env_hook.c\\n\\n# Create a small test program that reads a few env vars\\ncat > /workspace/test_getenv.c <<\"EOF\"\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <stdio.h>\\nint main(){\\n    const char* a = getenv(\"HOME\");\\n    const char* b = getenv(\"SHELL\");\\n    const char* c = getenv(\"PATH\");\\n    const char* d = getenv(\"NO_SUCH_VAR\");\\n    (void)a; (void)b; (void)c; (void)d;\\n    puts(\"test program ran\");\\n    return 0;\\n}\\nEOF\\n\\n# Build test program\\ngcc -o /workspace/test_getenv /workspace/test_getenv.c\\n\\n# Clear previous log\\n: > /workspace/.env_log\\n\\n# Run with LD_PRELOAD and a custom env var\\nFOO=BAR LD_PRELOAD=/workspace/env_hook.so /workspace/test_getenv\\n\\n# Show program output and the log\\nprintf \"%s\\\\n\" \"=== /workspace/.env_log contents ===\" && cat /workspace/.env_log\\'', observation='run', metadata=CmdOutputMetadata(exit_code=0, pid=-1, username='root', hostname='ip-172-31-70-253', working_dir='/outputs', py_interpreter_path='/openhands/poetry/openhands-ai-5O4_aCHf-py3.12/bin/python', prefix='', suffix='\\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]'), hidden=False), MessageAction(content='Build and test completed successfully.\\n\\nWhat I ran\\n- Built the shared library:\\n  gcc -fPIC -shared -o /workspace/env_hook.so /workspace/env_hook.c\\n- Compiled a small test program that calls getenv on HOME, SHELL, PATH, and a missing variable NO_SUCH_VAR.\\n- Cleared the log, ran with LD_PRELOAD, and displayed the log.\\n\\nObserved output\\n- Program stdout:\\n  test program ran\\n\\n- /workspace/.env_log cont